          %blockquote
            %p
              (graphics adapted from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/New+Foundations+for+TDA+--+Cohomotopy"} SS 22
          %p
            Here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curve"} curve
            indicates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and “gray” stands for the region
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi r
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_r \,\subset\, X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^1 \setminus B_r
          %p
            One sees on the left that if the cohomotopy class of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            at resolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/r
            is non-trivial, then there is at least one zero.
          %p#IntuitivelyClear
            In the situation on the right it is intuitively clear that a deformation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            with magnitude smaller than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            may move the curve/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph
            away from the horizontal 0-line. In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            this is the statement that in this case the
            = succeed "-map" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi gray
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi red
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/gray \to \mathbb{R}^1/red
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
            (here: a
            = succeed "-class)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomotopy"} cohomotopy
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/PersistentCohomotopy-TheIdea-220524b.gif", :width => "600"}/
